#   Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
#   This repo is worked on with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to CRLF in the
# working tree. For C sources that is harmless. For a shell script it is not: bash reads the
# trailing \r as part of each command and fails with `$'\r': command not found`, or silently
# passes an argument with a carriage return glued to the end of it. The script is not broken and
# does not look broken -- it is a checkout artifact, and it shows up on a fresh clone, which is
# the least convenient moment to meet it.
#
#   the three scripts here (install_freetype2.sh and the two ASan repro drivers) are all run
# under WSL or a Linux host, so every one of them is exposed.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
